In conclusion, this work addresses the issue of rate limit errors in language models, highlighting the main technical contributions as the identification of rate limit exceeded errors and the implementation of retry mechanisms. The key experimental results show that after five retries, a rate limit error occurs, with a limit of 100,000 tokens per day, and 99,964 tokens used, indicating that the model is approaching its token limit. Future work will involve exploring alternative models or service tiers to mitigate rate limit errors. 
